# Project documentation location

- Put **new monorepo-wide docs** (markdown guides, checklists, Word specs) in **`project-docs/`** unless the user specifies another path.
- Keep the **root `README.md`** as the repo entry point only; link into `project-docs/README.md` for the full index.
- **App-specific READMEs** stay under `apps/*`, `packages/*`, or `brand/` — do not move those into `project-docs/`.
- **Topic how-tos** (push setup, local APK, realtime) stay in **`docs/`** unless consolidating into `project-docs/` is requested.
- Doc generators (`scripts/generate-*-test-doc.py`) write `.docx` files to **`project-docs/`**.

When adding a new project doc, update **`project-docs/README.md`** and link from root **`README.md`** if it is essential onboarding material.
